      'en': 'Answer: <b>も いいですか</b>. B answers どうぞ, which <b>gives permission</b>, so A must be asking <b>\'may I use it?\'</b><br>Distractors: <b>もらえますか</b> and <b>くれませんか</b> both <b>ask the listener to do the action</b>, which would mean \'please use this chair\', but B replies どうぞ、使って ください (offering the chair to A), the opposite direction, so it does not connect; <b>は いけませんか</b> asks \'isn\'t it allowed?\', a protest or a check on a ban, and does not lead naturally to どうぞ.<br><b>Order of work: read the reply first.</b> If the reply is どうぞ (permission), think of てもいいですか.',
